GLYMUR DIAGNOSTIC (2026-07-30) — not for upstream.

Adds a module_param skip knob to bam_dma's late suspend/resume callbacks so the
suspend-reset suspect list can be bisected without a rebuild per experiment.

Context: /sys/power/pm_test bisects the ASUS Zenbook A16 (glymur) suspend path —
pm_test=devices SURVIVES, pm_test=platform hard-resets the SoC with no kernel
fault. Per kernel/power/suspend.c:529 vs :445, and with s2idle_ops NULL on
arm64, the delta is exactly dpm_suspend_late() + dpm_suspend_noirq(). Only three
drivers bound on this machine implement either, and bam_dma is the only one with
a *late* callback — so skipping it splits the suspect list 1-vs-2.

Suspend and resume are gated together to keep clk_prepare/clk_unprepare
balanced; an asymmetric skip misled the earlier msm bisect (bit 1).

Usage: bam_dma.glymur_skip_late=1 on the kernel cmdline (or write the sysfs
param, though the module cannot be unloaded live — refcount 2).

srcversion: CE55C844C523C937415AB26 -> 5124C49E285304DA2992079

--- a/drivers/dma/qcom/bam_dma.c	2026-07-30 14:26:49.812247809 -0400
+++ b/drivers/dma/qcom/bam_dma.c	2026-07-30 14:26:49.820231637 -0400
@@ -1451,10 +1451,33 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * GLYMUR DIAGNOSTIC (2026-07-30, not for upstream).
+ *
+ * pm_test bisects the ASUS Zenbook A16 suspend path to dpm_suspend_late() +
+ * dpm_suspend_noirq(): pm_test=devices survives, pm_test=platform hard-resets
+ * the SoC with no kernel fault. bam_dma is the only driver bound on this
+ * machine with a *late* callback, and it drops a clock there -- the same shape
+ * as the eDP PHY clk_bulk_disable_unprepare that was lethal in the display
+ * teardown. Skipping it splits the three-driver suspect list 1-vs-2.
+ *
+ * Suspend and resume are skipped TOGETHER so clk_prepare/clk_unprepare stay
+ * balanced; an asymmetric skip misled the earlier msm bisect (bit 1).
+ */
+static bool glymur_bam_skip_late;
+module_param_named(glymur_skip_late, glymur_bam_skip_late, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(glymur_skip_late,
+		 "GLYMUR DIAGNOSTIC: skip bam_dma late suspend/resume (default 0)");
+
 static int __maybe_unused bam_dma_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct bam_device *bdev = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
+	if (glymur_bam_skip_late) {
+		dev_info(dev, "GLYMUR: skipping bam_dma_suspend()\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
 	clk_unprepare(bdev->bamclk);
 
@@ -1466,6 +1489,11 @@
 	struct bam_device *bdev = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int ret;
 
+	if (glymur_bam_skip_late) {
+		dev_info(dev, "GLYMUR: skipping bam_dma_resume()\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	ret = clk_prepare(bdev->bamclk);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
